        "original_id": "c46c65cf-41bf-5dd3-a7eb-b7d8b19af46d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Chiltern Shakespeare Company\n- Works: Twelfth Night, She's the Man, Just One of the Guys, Big Fat Liar, Much Ado about Nothing, A Midsummer Night's Dream, As You Like It, The Taming of the Shrew, The Merchant of Venice, The Merry Wives of Windsor\n- People: William Shakespeare, Alexandra Breckenridge\n- Topics: Shakespeare adaptations, comedy films\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote the comedy play \"Twelfth Night, or What You Will\" around 1601–02 as Twelfth Night entertainment for the close of the Christmas season.\n- The Chiltern Shakespeare Company has recently produced \"Much Ado about Nothing,\" \"Twelfth Night,\" \"A Midsummer Night's Dream,\" \"As You Like It,\" \"The Taming of the Shrew,\" \"The Merchant of Venice,\" and \"The Merry Wives of Windsor.\"\n- The 2006 film \"She's the Man\" was inspired by William Shakespeare's play \"Twelfth Night\" and is a remake of the 1985 film \"Just One of the Guys.\"\n- Alexandra Breckenridge began her career with supporting roles in the teen comedy films \"Big Fat Liar\" in 2002 and \"She's the Man\" in 2006.",
